      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MODS (3) is the top pick after charging home to beat WARREGO by a length and a half over 1100m last start, following a close third behind TOKYO BANDIT. He's third-up, quick to back up, has Billy Cray aboard, and a solid record here, plus the extra distance should be manageable. WARREGO (2) is the main danger, having won well two starts ago in SC grade before chasing MODS home last time, with a win and a placing from three starts at this track. TEE GALLERIA (4) has a reliable placing profile, with a second in BM54 last start and a Class 2 third before, plus his record with Paul Shiers keeps him competitive. PAFITIS (7) has been close without winning, finishing third behind MODS last week and second as favourite prior, and the quick back-up offers a chance for a sharper finish.",
